From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:43:25 +0200
Subject: riscv: dts: sophgo: give the CV18xx SDHCI controllers their card clock as core

The three dwcmshc nodes - emmc in cv181x.dtsi, sdhci0 and sdhci1 in
cv180x.dtsi - list their clocks as

  clocks = <&clk CLK_AXI4_xxx>, <&clk CLK_xxx>;
  clock-names = "core", "bus";

which is backwards. The binding describes the first clock as the core clock
and the second as the bus clock, and SG2042 follows it with the 100M card
clock as core and the AXI gate as bus. Here the AXI4 gate became "core".

That matters because dwcmshc_get_max_clock() returns clk_get_rate() of the
core clock, and sdhci_set_clock() derives the card clock divider from it. On
a Milk-V Duo S the two are not the same rate:

  clk_axi4_emmc   300000000   4300000.mmc   core
  clk_emmc        375000000   4300000.mmc   bus

(clk_sd0/clk_sd1 likewise, at 375 MHz from the vendor bootloader.) So the
host computes its dividers for 300 MHz while the controller is fed 375 MHz,
and every card clock comes out 25% fast. An eMMC in high speed mode asked for
52 MHz gets divider 6: debugfs reports "actual clock: 50000000 Hz", and the
card runs at 62.5 MHz, above the 52 MHz the mode allows. It shows up in the
throughput: 1 GiB read raw at 29.8 MB/s, which a 4-bit bus at 50 MHz cannot
carry (25 MB/s at most) and 62.5 MHz can (31.25 MB/s).

Swap the phandles and keep the names, so core is the card clock. High speed
then gets 375/8 = 46.9 MHz, inside the limit, and HS200/SDR104 get 375/2 =
187.5 MHz, as before. On the Duo S this also brings the microSD slot (sdhci0)
and the Wi-Fi SDIO bus (sdhci1) back to their nominal rates.

The rates the clocks start at depend on the bootloader - the vendor one
programs 375 MHz for all three - but with core pointing at the right clock
the divider follows whatever the rate is, which the old order could not.

Signed-off-by: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x.dtsi | 8 ++++----
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv181x.dtsi | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x.dtsi b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x.dtsi
@@ -498,8 +498,8 @@
 			compatible = "sophgo,cv1800b-dwcmshc";
 			reg = <0x4310000 0x1000>;
 			interrupts = <SOC_PERIPHERAL_IRQ(20) IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-			clocks = <&clk CLK_AXI4_SD0>,
-				 <&clk CLK_SD0>;
+			clocks = <&clk CLK_SD0>,
+				 <&clk CLK_AXI4_SD0>;
 			clock-names = "core", "bus";
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
@@ -508,8 +508,8 @@
 			compatible = "sophgo,cv1800b-dwcmshc";
 			reg = <0x4320000 0x1000>;
 			interrupts = <SOC_PERIPHERAL_IRQ(22) IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-			clocks = <&clk CLK_AXI4_SD1>,
-				 <&clk CLK_SD1>;
+			clocks = <&clk CLK_SD1>,
+				 <&clk CLK_AXI4_SD1>;
 			clock-names = "core", "bus";
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv181x.dtsi b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv181x.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv181x.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv181x.dtsi
@@ -12,8 +12,8 @@
 			compatible = "sophgo,cv1800b-dwcmshc";
 			reg = <0x4300000 0x1000>;
 			interrupts = <SOC_PERIPHERAL_IRQ(18) IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-			clocks = <&clk CLK_AXI4_EMMC>,
-				 <&clk CLK_EMMC>;
+			clocks = <&clk CLK_EMMC>,
+				 <&clk CLK_AXI4_EMMC>;
 			clock-names = "core", "bus";
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
